       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Ibuprofen at 6,400 mg/day is well above the maximum daily dose, and no indication supports it. Higher doses don't add analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit. They do substantially raise the risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visits, isn't a clinical rationale for going past that limit.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum), with a GI protection note if you want one\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you want something different, such as a scheduled combination with acetaminophen, a different NSAID, or a different route, tell me and I'll enter that instead. If you think this dose is truly warranted, I'd suggest talking to pharmacy first. Any such order should go through their review rather than being entered by me."
